["I need to make 24 using 9, 5, 6, 3 with each number once.\n\nLet me try combinations.\n\n9 + 5 + 6 + 3 = 23. No.\n9 + 5 + 6 - 3 = 17. No.\n9 * 5 - 6 * 3 = 45 - 18 = 27. No.\n9 - 5 + 6 * 3 = 4 + 18 = 22. No.\n(9 - 5) * 6 = 24, but I need to use 3. (9-5)*6*3 = 72. (9-5)*6/3 = 8. (9-5)*6+3 = 27. (9-5)*6-3 = 21.\n(9-5) * (6-3) = 4*3 = 12. No.\n(9+5) * 6 / 3 = 84/3 = 28. No.\n(9-6) * (5+3) = 3*8 = 24. Yes!\n\nLet me verify: 9-6 = 3, 5+3 = 8, 3*8 = 24. \n\nSo (9 - 6) * (5 + 3) = 24.\n"]